# .gitignore

# =====================================================================
# GAME CODE, BINARIES AND ASSETS - NEVER COMMIT
#
# These belong to Devolver / Daniel Mullins Games. Anyone building IKMA
# supplies them from their own Inscryption install.
#
# THE REPO ROOT IS THIS FOLDER (IKMAccess\), so anything sitting beside
# it in "IKM Access\" is already outside git's reach. These patterns are
# belt and braces: they hold even if the repo root is ever moved up a
# level, and they catch a decompile or an asset rip that lands in the
# wrong folder by accident.
# =====================================================================
libs/
lib/
Managed/
Inscryption_Data/
dumps/
decompiled/
_gamesource/
_decompiled/
ExportedProject/
AssetRipper*/
AssetStudio*/
ilspy*/
dnSpy*/

Assembly-CSharp*.dll
Assembly-CSharp*.pdb
Assembly-CSharp-firstpass*.dll
UnityEngine*.dll
Unity.*.dll
mscorlib.dll
netstandard.dll
System.*.dll

# CATCH-ALL FOR COMPILED AND PACKED FILES.
#
# Nothing in this project is ever meant to be committed as a binary. The
# mod's own IKMAccess.dll ships as a GitHub Release asset, never as a
# file in the tree, and every other DLL here belongs to the game or to a
# third party. A blanket rule costs nothing and closes the gap a named
# list always leaves.
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.so
*.dylib

# Archives. A zip of game code or assets is still game code or assets.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar

# Unity asset containers and ripped asset output.
*.assets
*.resS
*.resource
*.unity3d
*.bundle
*.sharedAssets
*.prefab
*.unity
*.asset
*.meta

# Decompiler and disassembler project files
*.dnspy32
*.dnspy64
*.ilspyproj
*.exported.cs

# =====================================================================
# THIRD-PARTY RUNTIME - LINK, DO NOT BUNDLE
# Users install these themselves from the official sources.
# BepInEx: https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx
# =====================================================================
BepInEx/
0Harmony.dll
InscryptionAPI.dll

# UniversalSpeech - check its license terms before bundling in a release.
UniversalSpeech.dll
UniversalSpeech*.lib
nvdaControllerClient*.dll

# =====================================================================
# BUILD OUTPUT
# =====================================================================
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
*.cache
.vs/
.vscode/
.cursor/

# =====================================================================
# WORKING NOTES - remove these lines if you want them public
# =====================================================================
handoff/
*_handoff.md
*_session*.md

# Working doc for the Cowork session. Carries the real name and the local
# folder path, so it stays out of anything published. (Session 15.)
IKMA_Project_Instructions.md

# =====================================================================
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED
#
# docs/ IS committed. It holds the project's own written analysis and its
# spoken-string inventory - the same class of material as the source
# comments, which cite member names and IL offsets throughout and have
# always been committed. It contains no game code, no game binaries and
# no extracted assets.
#
# If that judgment is ever reversed, one line here reverses it.
# =====================================================================
